usage: mat [OPTION]... [FILE]...
Concatenate FILE(s) to standard output. With no FILE, or when FILE is
-, read standard input.

  -n            number all output lines
  -b            number nonempty output lines (overrides -n)
  -s            squeeze repeated empty lines
  -e            display $ at end of each line (implies -v)
  -t            display TAB as ^I (implies -v)
  -v            show nonprinting characters (^ and M- notation)
  -A            equivalent to -vet
  -E            display $ at end of each line
  -T            display TAB as ^I
  -u            (ignored; output is always unbuffered on the fast path)

Decorations (opt-in; piped output stays plain like cat):
  -p, --pretty         show the full frame (header, grid, numbers)
  -S, --chop-long-lines  do not wrap (same as --wrap=never)
      --style=LIST     numbers,grid,header,header-filesize,rule,snip
                       presets plain,default,full (e.g. full,-grid)
      --decorations=WHEN  auto|never|always
      --color=WHEN        auto|never|always
      --wrap=MODE         auto|never|character|word
      --tabs=N            expand tabs to N columns (0 = off)
      --terminal-width=N  columns for the frame
  -P, --no-paging      do not page output
      --paging=WHEN       auto|never|always (bespoke pager)

Line selection:
  -r, --line-range=RANGE  print only RANGE; repeat to accumulate.
                       N:M  :M  N:  -N: (last N)  N:+M  N::C (context)
  -H, --highlight-line=RANGE  emphasize lines (decorated output)
      --squeeze-limit=N   max blank lines kept under -s (default 1)

Encoding:
      --binary=WHEN       no-printing|as-text (decorated binary files)
      --strip-ansi=WHEN   auto|never|always (remove input escapes)

Syntax mapping (detection inputs; highlighting is a later sprint):
  -l, --language=NAME     force the syntax
  -m, --map-syntax=GLOB:NAME  map a filename glob to a syntax
      --ignored-suffix=.EXT   strip before extension detection
      --file-name=NAME    display/detection name for stdin
      --fallback-syntax=NAME  when detection fails
      --detect-syntax     print the detected syntax and exit

Config (defaults from /etc/mat/config, ~/.config/mat/config, $MAT_OPTS,
$MAT_STYLE/$MAT_TABS/$MAT_WRAP; the command line overrides):
      --no-config              ignore config files
      --config-file            print the config file path
      --config-dir             print the config directory
      --generate-config-file   print a config template

      --help    display this help and exit
      --version output version information and exit
